+        A byte operand multiplies AL into AX and divides AX into AL
+        (quotient) and AH (remainder); a word multiplies AX into DX:AX and
+        divides DX:AX into AX and DX; a dword uses EDX:EAX. Every form was
+        lifted as the dword one, so `mul cl` clobbered EDX and multiplied
+        all of EAX, and `div cl` divided EDX:EAX.
+
+        mul and imul publish CF = OF (the product does not fit the low half)
+        in _fb. The divisor is read once, before any write: `div eax` would
+        otherwise take the remainder by the new quotient.
+
